---
import SiteLayout from '../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const flow = 'Sandbox platform\n' +
  '├── ConnectionAgent Domain  ·  Agent / Runtime / Skills\n' +
  '├── Tool Plane              ·  discovery / gateway / common capabilities\n' +
  '├── Environment Plane       ·  env-core / simulated & real worlds / env-fabric\n' +
  '├── Evaluation              ·  bench-suite / bench-engine\n' +
  '├── Control / Surface       ·  control / console\n' +
  '└── Shared Foundation       ·  nodus\n' +
  '\nPlatform-level composition and compatibility governance.\n' +
  'Each component retains its own contract and fact authority.';
---
<SiteLayout title="Sandbox Platform Architecture" lang="en" description="Sandbox platform layers, component responsibilities, and cross-repository authority boundaries.">
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Sandbox / Architecture</span>
    <h1>Sandbox platform architecture</h1>
    <p class="lede">Sandbox is the product-level composition and governance layer for Agents, tools, environments, and evaluation. It defines how components work together, remain compatible, and form runnable experiments. Each component retains ownership of its implementation, contracts, and domain facts.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="grid"><div class="card wide">
    <h3>Platform layers</h3><pre><code>{flow}</code></pre>
    <p class="muted">This is the target architecture, not a claim that every component migration or end-to-end acceptance is complete. Current repository names may differ from target names; consult Sandbox migration records and owner repositories for status.</p>
  </div></div></section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Responsibilities by plane</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Plane</th><th>Responsibility</th><th>Main components (target taxonomy)</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>ConnectionAgent Domain</td><td>Agent Hosts, planning and routing, Skill source/build, governed execution, Outcome, Reconcile, and Recovery.</td><td><code>ca-agent</code>, <code>ca-runtime</code>, <code>ca-dsh</code>, <code>ca-nanobot</code>, <code>ca-skills</code>, <code>ca-skill-toolchain</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Tool Plane</td><td>Tool discovery and invocation protocols, gateway mapping, and cross-environment capabilities. The gateway does not own underlying business effects.</td><td><code>tool-mcp-gw</code>, <code>tool-common</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Environment Plane</td><td>Environment substrate, simulated or real worlds, authoritative source facts, external-system integration, network observation, and controlled intervention.</td><td><code>env-core</code>, <code>env-5gc-sim</code>, <code>env-5gc-real</code>, <code>env-fabric</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Evaluation</td><td>Evaluation assets, task freezing, execution attempts, evidence validity, Verdicts, and result analysis.</td><td><code>bench-suite</code>, <code>bench-engine</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Control / Surface</td><td>Select and compose resources, manage outer lifecycle and experiment runs, and provide the human-facing interface.</td><td><code>control</code>, <code>console</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Shared Foundation</td><td>Reusable domain-neutral mechanics without taking over domain semantics.</td><td><code>nodus</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Composition authority is not fact authority</h2>
    <p>Sandbox can register components, pin compatible versions, define compositions, and enforce system-level integration gates. That does not make the platform repository the source of every fact.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>ca-runtime</code> owns Runtime Outcomes for governed execution; Sandbox must not create a second writer.</li>
      <li>Environment owners own their world state and source facts; Sandbox does not replace them with a central state store.</li>
      <li>The Benchmark Engine forms Verdicts from frozen tasks and evidence rules; Sandbox does not adjudicate the same trial separately.</li>
      <li>Control manages outer resource and experiment lifecycle; that does not give it ownership of Environment state or Benchmark semantics.</li>
      <li>Console presents and operates platform capabilities but is not authoritative for underlying facts.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Environments and the system under test</h2>
    <p>Sandbox can compose simulated, real, and hybrid environments. An environment is where the system under test runs and is observed; it is not synonymous with a single simulator. The frozen EvaluationTask declares whether a trial includes the Agent, Runtime, tools, or an end-to-end composition. Repository names do not determine the test boundary.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Status and authoritative references</h2>
    <p>The target planes are established and some repositories have moved to their target names. Consumer migration and acceptance continue in stages. This page describes the target architecture and established responsibility boundaries; planned capabilities are not presented as delivered features.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/odango-chan/sandbox/blob/main/docs/architecture/sandbox.md">Sandbox architecture and boundaries</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/odango-chan/sandbox/blob/main/docs/architecture/repository-topology.md">Repository topology and migration names</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/odango-chan/sandbox/blob/main/docs/ownership.md">Sandbox ownership rules</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/odango-chan/connectionagent/blob/main/docs/architecture.md">Existing ConnectionAgent Domain architecture material</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
